  "title": "She Found Her College Sweetheart Homeless on a City Street—16 Years Ago, Her Husband Set Him Up",
  "description": "She knelt in the rain to pick up a homeless man&apos;s coins — and found herself looking at the boy she loved in college.<br><br>Sixteen years ago, Luke Bennett was a scholarship student at Northbrook who dreamed of building bridges, until a gold watch turned up in his bag and he was expelled for theft. Now he sits on a city sidewalk. When Hannah Caldwell recognizes him, her husband Spencer says Luke stole his watch back then — while the very same watch is still on Spencer&apos;s wrist.<br><br>Hannah gives Luke a job as groundskeeper at Larkspur Hill, her late father&apos;s vineyard estate. Behind a half-closed curtain, Luke hears plans that were never meant for him, and in a stuck desk drawer he finds a sealed letter he wrote sixteen years ago — the one Hannah never got. Then, at the couple&apos;s tenth anniversary party, Spencer mocks him in front of every guest, and Hannah&apos;s mother&apos;s diamond necklace disappears from the safe. Minutes later, it turns up in Luke&apos;s old bag. Same bag. Same trick.<br><br>👉 Watch till the end — a forgotten camera, a pair of chipped pliers, and a promise made on a stone bridge sixteen years ago are about to change everything.<br><br>If you love stories where quiet kindness wins and the truth finally comes out, subscribe for a new story every week.<br><br>This is a fictional story made for entertainment. All characters, places and events are invented.<br><br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/dramastory\">#DramaStory</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/secondchance\">#SecondChance</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/story\">#Story</a>",
